// "Col des Moufles": a snowy mountain pass (issue #19, redrawn for issue #109 after the guide
// « Conception des circuits », docs/GAME_DESIGN.md § 16). Original layout, about 1.3 km a lap,
// turning left: the start straight in the valley; three switchbacks up the face of the mountain
// (hairpins to the left, the right and the left: a lacet), 12 m up to the pass; on the pass, the
// corner of the risky jump (to the right, its inside a drop of 12 m) and the summit; a tight left
// turn, then the way down: a bulge (right 70°, left 140°, right 70°) whose hidden road runs
// straight behind a bank of snow; two more switchbacks at the foot of the mountain (left, right);
// the tight left corner that the snow path cuts, and the last corner. Five hairpins of 180° (a
// Normal bot drifts them), four tight turns of 90°, the S of the switchbacks and of the summit:
// no long soft curve, one long straight. The pieces of the shortcuts (the jump's corner, the
// bulge, the snow path's corner) are those of Prairie Pompon (#108), mirrored where the Col turns
// the other way.
//
// Drawn as a plan of straights and arcs, its points every 8 m along it (the parameters below
// follow them).
//
// Format: see src/track/data.rs. Positions along the track ("at", "from", "to") are spline
// parameters: 9.5 = halfway between points 9 and 10. Lateral "offset" goes from -1 (left
// edge of the road) to 1 (right edge). Point 0 is the start line; karts drive toward point 1
// (north, -Z), then turn left. The grid sits on the straight behind point 0.
(
    name: "Col des Moufles",
    // Dressing (issue #11): the snow (`assets/data/biomes.ron`: issue #109, giant firs and
    // needles of rock), the same every time (seed), and pieces placed by hand: nutcrackers at the
    // start line (beyond the posts of its arch, issue #79), a giant decorated fir by the grid,
    // needles of rock outside the switchbacks (they show the mountain from afar), a giant snowman
    // on the summit, a bank of snow that hides the hidden road (low: nothing high stands inside a
    // tight turn, GD § 14), reindeer at the foot of the mountain.
    biome: "Neige",
    // Issue #104: its music (`assets/data/music.ron`).
    music: "blossom-mountain",
    decor_seed: 19,
    // Issue #146: its own far decor, on top of the snow's: three giant summits that tower over the
    // pass, and a herd of giant reindeer in the far fields.
    far_decor: [
        Peaks(count: 3, distance: (120.0, 260.0), height: (170.0, 230.0), radius: (55.0, 80.0),
              sides: 6, color: (0.40, 0.44, 0.53), top: ((0.98, 0.99, 1.0), 120.0)),
        Pieces(models: ["holiday-kit/reindeer"], count: 6, height: (9.0, 12.0), radius: 5.0,
               distance: (60.0, 140.0), side: Inside),
    ],
    props: [
        (model: "holiday-kit/nutcracker", at: 0.0, side: Both, height: 3.5, radius: 0.9, gap: 1.8),
        (model: "holiday-kit/tree-decorated-snow", at: 162.5, side: Right, height: 16.0, radius: 5.0, gap: 1.0),
        (model: "nature-kit/rock_tallJ", at: 14.5, side: Right, height: 24.0, radius: 6.0, gap: 3.0),
        (model: "nature-kit/rock_tallH", at: 50.5, side: Right, height: 26.0, radius: 5.0, gap: 3.0),
